Good — the test can include `tsk/fs/tsk_fs_i.h` with `-I..` (tests have `-I.. -I$(srcdir)/..`).

Now write the code. Start with library changes.

### 1. `tsk/fs/tsk_fs.h`

Add to TSK_FS_FLS_FLAG_ENUM:
```c
        TSK_FS_FLS_HASH = 0x40,
        TSK_FS_FLS_MAC_M = 0x80,     ///< With TSK_FS_FLS_MAC: include modification time
        TSK_FS_FLS_MAC_A = 0x100,    ///< With TSK_FS_FLS_MAC: include access time
        TSK_FS_FLS_MAC_C = 0x200,    ///< With TSK_FS_FLS_MAC: include metadata change time
        TSK_FS_FLS_MAC_B = 0x400     ///< With TSK_FS_FLS_MAC: include creation (birth) time
```
And a new public enum for the mask:
```c
    /**
     * \ingroup fslib
     * Flags to select which timestamp types are included in mactime (body file)
     * timeline output. ...
     */
    enum TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_ENUM {
        TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_M = 0x1,
        TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_A = 0x2,
        TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_C = 0x4,
        TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_B = 0x8,
        TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_ALL = 0xf
    };
    typedef enum TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_ENUM TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_ENUM;
```

Where do enum docs go — check existing comment style in tsk_fs.h enum: they don't have per-member comments mostly. Keep brief comments.

### 2. `tsk/fs/tsk_fs_i.h`

Add declaration after tsk_fs_name_print_mac_md5:
```c
    extern uint8_t tsk_fs_name_print_mac_md5_mask(FILE *, const TSK_FS_FILE *,
        const char *, const TSK_FS_ATTR * fs_attr, const char *, int32_t,
        const unsigned char *, uint8_t time_mask);
```

### 3. `tsk/fs/fs_name.c`

Refactor: tsk_fs_name_print_mac_md5 keeps signature, calls mask version with TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_ALL. New function contains the old body plus mask logic.

For the time fields, current code (FNAME variant):
```c
            if (fs_file->meta->time2.ntfs.fn_atime)
                tsk_fprintf(hFile, "%" PRIu32 "|",
                    fs_file->meta->time2.ntfs.fn_atime - time_skew);
            else
                tsk_fprintf(hFile, "%" PRIu32 "|",
                    fs_file->meta->time2.ntfs.fn_atime);
```
I'll add a static helper above:

```c
/* Print a single mactime body-file time field.  If 'include' is 0 the
 * field is emitted as 0 (i.e. filtered out).  'sep' is appended after
 * the value (use 0 for the final field). */
static void
print_mac_time(FILE * hFile, time_t t, int32_t time_skew, uint8_t include,
    char sep)
{
    uint32_t val = include ? (uint32_t) t : 0;
    if (val)
        tsk_fprintf(hFile, "%" PRIu32 "%c", val - time_skew, sep);
    else if (sep)
        tsk_fprintf(hFile, "%" PRIu32 "%c", val, sep);
    else
        tsk_fprintf(hFile, "%" PRIu32, val);
}
```
Hmm wait, when val nonzero and sep==0 → "%c" with 0 char prints a NUL byte! Fix: 

```c
static void
print_mac_time(FILE * hFile, time_t t, int32_t time_skew, uint8_t include,
    int with_sep)
{
    uint32_t val = include ? (uint32_t) t : 0;
    if (val)
        tsk_fprintf(hFile, "%" PRIu32, val - time_skew);
    else
        tsk_fprintf(hFile, "%" PRIu32, val);
    if (with_sep)
        tsk_fprintf(hFile, "|");
}
```
Cleaner. 

Wait, original prints `fs_file->meta->atime - time_skew` where atime is time_t — printed with PRIu32. My cast to uint32_t matches existing behavior (they pass time_t to %u effectively... actually passing 64-bit time_t to PRIu32 varargs is technically UB but works on LE; my explicit cast is cleaner and behavior-compatible for values that fit).

Hmm, careful: `val - time_skew` — original computes `atime - time_skew` in time_t (signed 64-bit) then prints as u32. If atime < skew, original gives huge u32. Mine: uint32_t - int32 → int arithmetic... `val - time_skew`: uint32_t and int32_t → both converted to uint32_t? Usual arithmetic conversions: uint32_t vs int32_t (same rank) → unsigned. Result wraps — matches original low-32-bits behavior. OK good.

Skip logic at function start:
```c
    if (time_mask != TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_ALL) {
        uint8_t have = 0;
        if (fs_file->meta) {
            if ((fs_attr) && (fs_attr->type == TSK_FS_ATTR_TYPE_NTFS_FNAME)) {
                if (((time_mask & TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_A) && fs_file->meta->time2.ntfs.fn_atime) ...) have = 1;
            } else {
                ...meta->atime/mtime/ctime/crtime
            }
        }
        if (!have)
            return 0;
    }
```
Return 1 at end.

But wait — the function currently prints the hash first, then name, etc. The skip check must happen before ANY output. Put the check at the very top after the NULL checks. 

Note: when meta==NULL and mask != ALL → skip (return 0). When mask==ALL → legacy behavior (prints zeros). Good.

### 4. `tsk/fs/fls_lib.c`

In printit MAC branch:
```c
    if (fls_data->flags & TSK_FS_FLS_MAC) {
        uint8_t time_mask = 0;
        uint8_t printed;
        if (fls_data->flags & TSK_FS_FLS_MAC_M) time_mask |= TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_M;
        if (fls_data->flags & TSK_FS_FLS_MAC_A) time_mask |= TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_A;
        if (fls_data->flags & TSK_FS_FLS_MAC_C) time_mask |= TSK_FS_MAC_TYPE_C;
